Yes, that is the information you have in your input file.  From the
latter you can see that there is one probeset targeting each strand.

The UGP file format does not provide strand information.  I needed by
your analysis?

> 3          10  3134605
> 4          10  3134605
> 5          10  3134884
> 6          10  3134884
> 7          10  3185734
> 8          10  3185734
> 9          10  3185804
> 10         10  3185804
>
> Does it look correct to you, so far?

Yes.

Next step is to setup an UFL file.  Have a look at Page 'Unit Fragment
Length (UFL) files':

  http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/web/unit-fragment-length-ufl-files

That example code is not complete for your setup, but try to do the
same as you did for the UGP file using importFrom().

Please reply with you script here for future references.
(Unfortunately, we cannot update the pages, cf.
http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/.  We are working on
setting up a new site to solve this).

/Henrik

