Hi Yu Chuan.

Some comments below.

On 3-Nov-09, at 12:36 PM, Yu Chuan wrote:

> Hi all,
>
> Follow up the below discussion....I am also trying to get the
> chromosome locations for the genes on a HuEx-1_0-st-v2 dataset.

Have a look at the section "Current NetAffx Annotation Files" at:
http://www.affymetrix.com/products_services/arrays/specific/exon.affx#1_4

Those CSV files go a long way to getting you what you need.

> I used the core CDF file HuEx-1_0-st-v2,coreR3,A20071112,EP.cdf made
> by Elizabeth for pre-processing using aroma.affymetrix. At the end I
> got a matrix of transcript-level  expression values with the first 5
> columns/rows as
>
>> trFit[1:5,1:5]
>  unitName groupName unit group cell
> 1  2315251   2315252    1     1    1
> 2  2315373   2315374    2     1    3
> 3  2315554   2315586    3     1    7
> 4  2315633   2315638    4     1   22
> 5  2315674   2315690    5     1   30
>
> Based on what EP suggested below, is it correct that I should have
> used the Ensembl cdf that Mark has created during the pre-processing
> step if I want to use biomaRt package to get the gene annotations?

It doesn't matter what CDF you use, you can still use biomaRt/
GenomeGraphs to pull down annotation information.  You just need
chromosome coordinates, which you can get from the CSV file from
Affy.  Or, see below.

> Or,
> is there any way that I can get the chromosome locations for each
> unitName using biomaRt package directly based on what I already have
> here? It seems that biomaRt package can also take Affy HuEx 1_0 st v2
> IDs for searching Ensembl database, however, I don't think the
> unitName above are Affy HuEx 1_0 st v2 IDs, right?

You'll have to look up the biomaRt details to do this exactly, but
here is a quick example (using groupNames i.e. probeset ids, not
transcript cluster ids):

 >      mart<-useDataset("hsapiens_gene_ensembl",mart)Checking
attributes ... ok
Checking filters ... ok
 >
getBM
(attributes
=
c
("affy_huex_1_0_st_v2
","hgnc_symbol","strand","transcript_start","chromosome_name"),
filters="affy_huex_1_0_st_v2",values=c("2315252","2315374"), mart=mart)
   affy_huex_1_0_st_v2 hgnc_symbol strand transcript_start
chromosome_name
1             2315374      FAM87B      1
752751               1
2             2315374      FAM87A     -1
325934               8

Cheers,
Mark

