Hi,

sorry for the delay - I'm on the road.  I've checked and I get the
same error using importFrom(ufl, dat, ...) when 'ufl' is an
AromaUflFile.  I'll try to fix this bug soon.

In the meanwhile, you can revert to manually assign the values of the
'ufl' file.  Below is an example how you can do it.  Note that you
have to retrieve the 'unitNames' and the fragment lengths
yourself/manual from your input file.  The example does not cover how
to do that, but you can use readDataFrame() for TabularTextFile to do
this conveniently, e.g.

filenameUfl_SNP <- "mDIV.annot.csv";
pathUfl <- "annotationData/chipTypes/mDIV/";
datUfl_SNP <- TabularTextFile(filenameUfl_SNP, path=pathUfl);

colClassPatterns <- c("^Probe ID$"="character", "^NspI Fragment
Size$"="integer", "^StyI Fragment Size$"="integer");
df <- readDataFrame(datUfl_SNP, colClassPatterns=colClassPatterns);

That will read exactly those columns into a data.frame (and nothing
else in case the file is big).

Now to the UFL example...

Example#1 - Manually assign values

cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType("GenomeWideSNP_6");

# Creates an empty UFL file for this CDF and with two enzymes.
ufl <- AromaUflFile$allocateFromCdf(cdf, tags="HB20091111", nbrOfEnzymes=2);
print(ufl);
AromaUflFile:
Name: GenomeWideSNP_6
Tags: HB20091111
Full name: GenomeWideSNP_6,HB20091111
Pathname: annotationData/chipTypes/GenomeWideSNP_6/GenomeWideSNP_6,HB20091111.ufl
File size: 7.08 MB (7424418 bytes)
RAM: 0.00 MB
Number of data rows: 1856069
File format: v1
Dimensions: 1856069x2
Column classes: integer, integer
Number of bytes per column: 2, 2
Footer: <platform>Affymetrix</platform><chipType>GenomeWideSNP_6</chipType>
Chip type: GenomeWideSNP_6
Platform: Affymetrix
# The UFL file is all empty

# The CDF names of some units that we know the fragment lengths of
(from other sources)
unitNames <- c("SNP_A-4214434", "SNP_A-2005029", "SNP_A-2005128",
"CN_065226", "CN_568310");

# Identify the unit indices (defined by the CDF) of these units
units <- indexOf(cdf, names=unitNames);
print(units);
[1]    1081    1082    1083 1506902 1506903

print(ufl[units,]);
  length length.02
1     NA        NA
2     NA        NA
3     NA        NA
4     NA        NA
5     NA        NA

# Assign fragment lengths for the first enzyme of these units
ufl[units,1] <- c(421, 510, NA, 939, 368);
print(ufl[units,]);
  length length.02
1    421        NA
2    510        NA
3     NA        NA
4    939        NA
5    368        NA

# Assign fragment lengths for the first enzyme of these units
ufl[units,2] <- c(1171, 520, 445, NA, 1974);
print(ufl[units,]);
  length length.02
1    421      1171
2    510       520
3     NA       445
4    939        NA
5    368      1974

Thus, SNP 'SNP_A-4214434' (unit #1081) is hybridized to the array via
fragments from both enzymes with lengths 421 and 1171 bp,
respectively.   CN locus 'CN_065226' (unit #1506902), on the other
hand, is hybridized to the array via a 939-bp long fragment from the
first enzyme only.

Hope this helps

Henrik

