Anita,

as noted by Henrik, there had been recurrent problems with the binary
installations. I run aroma on multiple Macs under 10.6 (64-bit, R
2.9.0 or 2.10 branch from http://r.research.att.com/), and have been
successful with source installation attempts of the different
components (not sure about the most recent status):

install.packages("matrixStats", type="source", repos="http://R-Forge.R-
project.org <http://project.org>")
install.packages("sfit", type="source", repos="http://R-Forge.R-
project.org <http://project.org>")
install.packages("aroma.core")
source("http://bioconductor.org/biocLite.R")
biocLite("digest")

and/or:

source("http://www.braju.com/R/hbLite.R")
hbLite("R.filesets")
hbLite("aroma.core")

... before trying hbinstall.

I don't use EBImage, though (but that wasn't your problem ...).

Best,

Michael.

